    "minides": "The iconic short-wheelbase Defender — 3-door, compact, and ferociously capable. 900mm water wading, Terrain Response 2, twin-speed transfer case, and the 2025 Pivi Pro Gen 2 update.",
    "description": "The Defender 90 is the iconic 3-door, short-wheelbase version of Land Rover's most capable SUV. It is offered in India in a single P300 variant powered by the 2.0-litre turbocharged 4-cylinder petrol producing 296 PS and 400 Nm, paired with an 8-speed ZF automatic and full-time AWD. Key Defender 90 attributes include its 2587 mm short wheelbase, 3-door configuration, 397-litre boot, and all the off-road hardware of its 5-door siblings — 900 mm water wading, electronic air suspension with 5 ride height modes, Terrain Response 2, twin-speed transfer case with low range, and lockable centre differential. The 2025 update brings a 13.1-inch Pivi Pro Gen 2 touchscreen, revised cabin finishes, and improved NVH. Level 2 ADAS, 360-degree ClearSight camera, and the full JLR connected services suite are standard."
  },
